1
00:00:01,100 --> 00:00:06,477
At large venues, crowd pressure can build faster than operations teams can see it.

2
00:00:06,427 --> 00:00:12,889
A queue at an entrance, concession, or exit can become a dangerous bottleneck before anyone has the full picture.

3
00:00:12,889 --> 00:00:15,814
CrowdFlow Optimiser closes that gap.

4
00:00:15,814 --> 00:00:20,141
Give it a venue layout, expected attendance, and event schedule.

5
00:00:20,141 --> 00:00:29,516
It simulates movement, blends signals from cameras, turnstiles, Wi-Fi, lidar, and opted-in app pings, then turns them into one live view.

6
00:00:29,516 --> 00:00:33,231
On the control-room map, density becomes a heat layer.

7
00:00:33,231 --> 00:00:40,708
The system ranks active bottlenecks, forecasts risks up to forty-five minutes ahead, and recommends the next operational action.

8
00:00:40,708 --> 00:00:45,118
Under the hood, a capacity-aware crowd model follows the event schedule.

9
00:00:45,118 --> 00:00:52,406
Sensor confidence updates the state, while congestion-aware pathfinding compares the shortest path with the safest available route.

10
00:00:52,406 --> 00:00:59,434
Teams can test closures, staffing, emergency scenarios, and multiple circuits before changing the real venue.

11
00:00:59,434 --> 00:01:02,193
Guidance does not stop at the dashboard.

12
00:01:02,193 --> 00:01:06,002
Spectators receive quieter routes and timely nudges.

13
00:01:06,002 --> 00:01:14,222
And where connectivity is weak, the companion mesh can relay compact, anonymous reroutes between nearby phones over Bluetooth and Wi-Fi.

14
00:01:14,222 --> 00:01:21,250
The result is a closed loop: sense, predict, reroute, and verify — before a crowd becomes a crisis.

15
00:01:21,250 --> 00:01:23,373
CrowdFlow Optimiser.

16
00:01:23,373 --> 00:01:26,179
Safer movement, in real time.
